<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- CHANGED 6 Oct 2026 - flattened, and paging REMOVED.

     HISTORY, because the reason is not obvious from the current state and the
     obvious-looking alternative has already been tried and failed twice.

     1. Originally this was the only one of the ten widget layouts with a nested
        ViewGroup and a bare View divider, and it was the only widget that would
        not inflate at all - "Can't load widget" on a black background, in the
        picker AND on the home screen. Flattening it fixed that, verified on device.

     2. Swipeable pages were then added (ViewFlipper, three pages) to show more
        data without a tap. That ALSO failed to render - on the owner's device,
        from the same build that passes every test. It re-introduced nested
        containers, which is the one thing that demonstrably breaks this widget.

     So the mechanism is now established by experiment rather than assumed: NESTED
     CONTAINERS IN A WIDGET RemoteViews LAYOUT DO NOT INFLATE HERE. It was never
     proven after the first fix and this commit is where it becomes real.

     Paging is therefore not viable with RemoteViews on this setup, and the way to
     show more data is to make ONE flat card carry more fields. Which is what this
     is: no container inside the root, and more content, rather than more pages.

     What paging DID leave behind, and is kept because it costs nothing here:
     - the appointment TIME, as its own field (KEY_APPT_VISIT_TIME), so the card
       can show a time at all. That was one of the reasons for wanting more data.
     - no reveal button. The old one fired a deep link resolving to an action
       nothing performs, so tapping it only opened the app. It is gone rather than
       fixed, because it implied a permanent-unmask that the provider's own
       comment already called security theatre - and with a single flat card there
       is nothing to reveal, because the privacy tier decides what is on screen.

     Layout order below is the clinic-visit order the Clinic Card screen uses, so
     the widget and the card agree: what you need at reception first, identifiers
     after. -->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:padding="16dp"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_background"
    android:gravity="center">

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_title"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:text="Clinic Card"
        android:textSize="16sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
        android:textStyle="bold" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_date"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
        android:text="No upcoming appointment"
        android:textSize="14sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_good"
        android:textStyle="bold" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_visit_time"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="2dp"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="13sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_location"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_accent"
        android:textStyle="bold" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_clinic_num"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_tests"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_muted" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_doctype"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="2dp"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_muted" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_clinic_nhs_num"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="2dp"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_muted"
        android:visibility="gone" />
</LinearLayout>